  "configuration_id": "config_015",
  "reason": "The current best (config_041, 0.7250 acc) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. The image encoder and aggregation choices are now well-characterized (vit_l >> resnet50; transformer > avgpool), but the RNA encoder has only been tested as scvi_n200 in the top-performing setup. Config_015 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) isolates the RNA encoder variable by swapping scvi_n200 for scgpt while holding all other factors constant. scgpt is a fundamentally different learned representation (generative vs. variational), so it may capture complementary biological signal that could push accuracy above 0.725. This is the highest-value exploration step: it either confirms scvi_n200 is optimal (freeing us to exploit the current best) or reveals a new direction with 4 experiments remaining. Expected cost: ~4.0–4.5 GPU hours, comparable to config_041 (3.60 h) since the dominant costs (ViT-L image encoder, transformer aggregation) are unchanged; scgpt is slightly heavier than scvi_n200 but the difference is modest relative to the image-side compute."
}

